  message: "Partial fix in PR #2557: added _short_name_penalty() to Haskell analyzer (same pattern as Scala PR #2525). Single-letter names get 0.15x confidence, two-letter get 0.50x. False edges from f/g/x/n are now easily filterable. Item remains open — top-level single-letter function extraction still happens, this just reduces confidence on the call edges."  # f0bf
